WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:01.040
- All right, Boogie.

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:05.560
So, with your Comedy Slam, which is
hilarious. I had the chance to watch it.

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:07.080
Whenever I'm telling people about it,

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:11.560
they're almost surprised that
you are, like, a funny, silly guy.

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:13.600
So would you describe yourself as that?

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.560
- I mean, I am.

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:21.040
I mean, it's funny you say that because, you
know, usually the only time that I'm seen is

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:22.560
during my occupation.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:26.480
So it's not really about
fun and games at that point—well, for me.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.880
I take the game seriously.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:32.520
But outside of the lines, I'm a
goofy, laid-back guy.

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:34.640
So, I enjoy comedy,

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:36.800
I enjoy laughing,
and I enjoy good vibes.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:37.880
So, that's what I'm about.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:38.560
-Now, I know

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:42.160
obviously you have some
hilarious guys in your special.

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:46.400
Tell me about them and what makes
them, you know, very special and funny guys.

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:53.120
- Well, you know, guys like Mike Epps,
Red Grant and Gary Owen, they've

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:56.680
been in the game for a long time. When
it comes to the younger guys, you know,

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:01.160
the Karlous Miller, and not necessarily
young in age, but just young in the game.

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:02.360
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
22
00:01:02,960 --&gt; 00:01:06,320
You know, they bring that next
generation of funny, which,

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:08.120
I always want that combination.

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:11.200
I want some of the older, OG guys
in the game and the new and up-and-coming.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:14.200
So that's kinda how I go about it.

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:16.800
- I hear that you are also
a bit of a jokester.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:18.160
Would you say that's true?

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:19.520
- Yeah.

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:21.000
I like to joke a lot actually, so.

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:22.080
- OK,

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:23.760
so I'm putting you on the spot with this.

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:28.560
I'm not asking you to tell me what the
exact joke is, but give me the gist,

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:28.920
OK?

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:34.200
I'm gonna name an NBA player, and you tell
me if you were making a joke about them,

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.240
what it would be along the lines of,

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:38.960
OK?
- Oh, come on!

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.680
- If we're doing comedy, DeMarcus,
we’re doing comedy.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:44.240
- Ohhh, naw,

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:45.520
that's crazy.

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:47.360
- Are you ready?

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:50.040
- Yeah, shoot.

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:56.560
- It's only two or three. OK.
- All right, all right.
- John Wall.
- The USA, the USA picture.

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:01.960
- [Laughing] And I assume you joke
about that a lot with him.

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:04.000
- Yes.
- OK.

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:07.520
Anthony Davis.
- The unibrow, obviously.

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:09.560
- [Laughing] OK.

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:14.640
LeBron James.
- I mean, the typical hair jokes about Bron.

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:15.000
So—
- [Laughing] OK.

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:23.520
Last one.
- OK.
- Steph Curry.
- That mouthpiece, man.

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:25.160
I feel bad for it.

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:28.640
- Always hanging out, always hanging out.
- Just, yeah.

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:32.360
- Shifting gears a little bit,

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:36.080
I think you saw that I spoke
to Mikey Williams a couple

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:41.040
weeks ago about HBCUs and the
possibility of him going to an HBCU.

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:43.760
And you are a player that
he specifically mentioned as

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:47.240
somebody who reached out to him
in support and encouragement.

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:49.760
Tell me about that
conversation with Mikey.

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:55.240
- You know, I basically sent him a
message saying, “You know, you got a chance

00:02:55.240 --> 00:03:01.600
to, you know, change sports as a
whole, start a trend that should

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:02.880
have already, you know, happened.”

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:07.760
You know, looking back
on it now, I wish I had that

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:10.440
opportunity to, you know,
do it the right way,

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:15.800
in my opinion. The attention, the
energy that a kid like Mikey

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:17.800
could take to any HBCU would,

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:21.120
like I said, change the, you know,
face of college sports.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:26.000
I had a chance to be on campus at Howard,
and I guess it was a time where, you

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:28.880
know, people may have been switching
classes, whatever the case may be.

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:34.600
And it was just like—I was, like, in awe
of, like, how many, like, blacks.

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:36.520
I've never seen it in my life.

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:38.720
- Yeah.
- And I was just in awe.

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:43.200
So, with that being said, I'm like, “Man.”
Like, even in that moment, I'm like,

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:47.720
“Damn, I should've, you know, I should've came
to Howard,” or whatever the case may be.

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:51.800
- Obviously anybody who has followed your
career knows that you went to Kentucky.

00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:56.320
So I guess my question is
what has caused the change?

00:03:56.360 --> 00:03:59.600
Meaning, what do you understand
now that maybe you didn't

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:02.600
understand then?
- The business.

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:07.360
And it's sad to say, but even
college, it's a business.

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:13.560
You know, obviously the athletes don't
benefit from it, but everything around

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:17.320
it is a business, and it's a reason they
want those kids at the school that could

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:21.920
easily be at HBCU with that same type of
attention, with that same type of income.

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:22.080
And,

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:24.200
and it’s well-deserved.

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:26.240
- It's gonna be really
interesting to see,

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:31.440
and I think that it gives us a lot
of pride and I think hope to know that the

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:34.600
younger generation is looking to do that

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:36.800
and the steps that
they're taking right now.

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:38.600
So, I totally agree.
- Absolutely.

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:39.280
- Absolutely.
- Absolutely.

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:43.440
- I want you to put on your analyst
hat. Give me your predictions.

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:46.000
- OK.
- Who's winning the championship this year?

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:47.200
- I don't know.

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:49.520
I got asked this question earlier.

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:50.800
I honestly don't know.

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:53.480
If it was the regular
season, it was playing out,

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:59.160
you know, the way it was, I think the
Lakers. But with the current situation

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:00.920
and everything that's into play,

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:07.440
I mean, all it takes is a guy to test
positive, and it changes a whole series.

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:09.960
Everybody has the same opportunity.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:12.240
So you can't say it's,

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:17.280
this is a, you know, “championship,
put it to the side,” because that's not true.

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:23.600
So, but it is teams that now have
a chance that didn't have one before.

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:26.480
I'll be tuned in, to say the
least, because I'm excited.

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:30.120
I feel like it's gonna be a team
that nobody expects.

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:32.400
- What is it gonna be like
playing without fans?

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:34.800
Like, what do you think the
guys are thinking right now?

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:39.600
What can you not say on the court
because everybody might hear it?

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:48.160
- The words will be very limited
at this point.

